  "reading": "On PMC_VQA the 32B answers 'A' on 23.3% of items where 'A' is gold 13.2% of the time, and it is right only 27.6% of the time when it says 'A' against 64.3% / 68.8% when it says B / C. 37.5% of ALL its errors are made while predicting A. That is the structured, answer-position-shaped error mode a cyclic-permutation ensemble is supposed to cancel, and it is why Attack 2 was worth running. It is a DIAGNOSTIC of headroom, NOT a result: an A-preference could equally be a fallback-under-uncertainty habit, in which case averaging over rotations moves the error rather than removing it."
